{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "money",
  "name": "Money",
  "description": "Where your money went — a personal ledger as a projection of the vault. Import a bank or card statement (CSV, OFX or QFX) and see spending by category against a monthly plan, cash flow, and balances checked against the balances your statements state. An account is the vault's own account entity and an imported line its own transaction, followed from the statement the member imported; the app adds your names, rules, plans and checkpoints. A line is never edited, only named, filed under a category or voided; importing the same file twice writes nothing; a possible duplicate or transfer is proposed and never decided for you. Every balance, total and forecast is derived at read time — nothing is stored — and nothing is ever added across currencies. The statement itself is read once and never kept. No data of its own — revoke the grant and the app goes dark.",
  "version": "0.2.0",
  "iconKey": "Coin",
  "colorKey": "indigo",
  "vault": {
    "why": "Reads your accounts and transactions to show where the money went, and files the statements you import.",
